rule: session-map
why: RULES.md rule 7 requires each line to contain a file name ending in .jsonl matching an existing session file; the final line has prose only and names no .jsonl, so FAIL even though final.jsonl exists (brief: "Final testing and verification: <which session, and where>").
expect: fail
file: submission/planning.jsonl
| {"type":"user","text":"decompose the routing console"}
file: submission/correction.jsonl
| {"type":"user","text":"the retry plan is wrong, stop"}
file: submission/final.jsonl
| {"type":"user","text":"run the tests and report"}
file: SUBMISSION.md
| Session map:
| - Initial planning or decomposition: planning.jsonl, from the first message to the task list
| - Most important correction or change of direction: correction.jsonl, where the retry plan is rejected
| - Final testing and verification: the last session in the export, near the end
